cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or the accompanying grading and analysis code,
  please cite it as below. When the associated article is published, please
  cite the article as well (see the notes field).
type: dataset
title: >-
  Verification-Surface Dataset: 1,116 Controlled Web-Application Builds by
  Six LLMs under Eight Tool Configurations
authors:
  - family-names: Mehta
    given-names: Achint
    email: achintmehta@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4192-8750"
version: 1.3.2
date-released: "2026-10-06"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21961590   # concept (all-versions) DOI; resolves to latest release
repository-code: "https://github.com/achintmehta/verification-surface-dataset"
license: CC-BY-4.0
# The author-written scripts are MIT-licensed; see LICENSE for the split.
keywords:
  - large language models
  - coding agents
  - verification
  - agent tooling
  - software engineering
  - controlled experiment
  - dataset
abstract: >-
  1,116 web applications built by six frontier language models under eight
  verification-tool configurations (from no checking tools to full shell
  plus screenshots), with byte-identical prompts proven by cryptographic
  fingerprints. Includes every artifact as shipped, complete per-run
  tool-call logs, machine grades from behavioral probes, condition-blind
  human rubric scores for all 1,116 runs, hand-audited launch-failure
  classifications, three SHA256-sealed dataset snapshots, the pre-specified
  statistical analysis plan with its committed code and complete output,
  and the grading instrument needed to re-grade every artifact.
notes: >-
  Companion dataset to the article "The reach of a verification tool
  decides its value: A controlled study of verification surface, artifact
  quality, and cost in AI coding agents" (A. Mehta, under review, 2026).
  The dataset of record is freeze-20260720/; freeze-20260716/ and
  freeze-20260703/ are superseded snapshots retained for provenance.
